1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,931
His AI agent finds a useful developer dataset for $10.

2
00:00:04,931 --> 00:00:09,204
John wants the file, but he doesn't want to hand over control of his wallet.

3
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:13,887
An agent shouldn't have unrestricted spending power.

4
00:00:13,887 --> 00:00:19,309
John wants to buy this one file, not give an agent permission to spend whenever it wants.

5
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:25,467
John sees the seller, the $10 price and the file he's getting.

6
00:00:25,467 --> 00:00:30,401
He sets a maximum source spend of 11 USDC and approves this one purchase.

7
00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:38,316
John sends about $10.11 from his Arbitrum wallet.

8
00:00:38,316 --> 00:00:45,212
NEAR Intents handles the cross-chain payment, and RouteTill verifies that the merchant received exactly $10 on Base.

9
00:00:56,450 --> 00:01:04,426
RouteTill verifies the merchant payment, delivers the correct dataset exactly once, and issues a signed Purchase Passport anyone can check.

10
00:01:11,450 --> 00:01:14,190
Judges can also try five security checks.

11
00:01:14,190 --> 00:01:18,892
RouteTill rejects changed recipients, over-limit payments and reused approvals.

12
00:01:18,892 --> 00:01:21,469
Twenty notifications produce one entitlement.

13
00:01:21,469 --> 00:01:23,745
Tampered evidence fails verification.

14
00:01:25,450 --> 00:01:26,832
John got the right file.

15
00:01:26,832 --> 00:01:28,039
The seller got paid.

16
00:01:28,039 --> 00:01:29,560
And RouteTill has the proof.
